# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/fusion-2 window (the prefill levers on the ship stack: the prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, WPP, and the 13x10 matmul grids, M1; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq lever needs its binary; every arm without the flag runs that binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# PL1 (TIMED, the COMBINED prefill ABAB, first pair): the LEVERS (B1): the combined arm plus QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ=1 and QWEN_FAST_GRID13=1, UNPROFILED, with
# C2_TELEMETRY=1. prefill_ladder_solo: four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, ONE request at a time with nothing else running, a
# 16-token answer: the time to first token and the prefill rate of each rung. Every boot a fresh reset, one tag at a time. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this
# job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ: c2_smoke_check clean (a lever boot also has its engaged lines and no fell-back line; a
# control boot has none of the lever's lines), no stall; then python3 -B scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py <control results> --second <lever results> for the pairs (PC1,
# PL1) and (PC2, PL2): the TTFT of the lever over the control per rung (a ratio below 1 is faster), the prefill rate, and the answer text of every rung equal between the
# arms (greedy text cannot depend on the prefill grid or the SDPA core layout). The control-to-control spread (PC1 against PC2) is the floor a gain has to beat. ESTIMATES
# TO BEAT (not measurements): oneq alone -7.9 s at the 131,072 rung and -29.8 s at the 253,920 rung (card M: the per-layer prefill SDPA 0.50x of the served call at
# 131k..254k), grid13's prefill matmuls -0.4 to -1.5 s (central -1.0 s) at 131,072 and about -2 s at 253,920 (the 85.7 of 266 ms of non-SDPA kernel time of a 2,048-row
# chunk on 8 rows of output tiles a core instead of 6); against ~36.8 s and ~98 s today the combined arm is about 28 s and 66 s if the gains add (they act on different ops
# of the same chunk, the SDPA and the three all-gather matmuls, so they add unless neither leaves the other cores or bandwidth). The 4k and 32k rungs move by under a
# second. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter
# holding it, power, current, temperature); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs
# on the host and is not part of any arm; it is on every leg so the pairs stay paired. A gain that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not
# the lever. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes, the solo ladder 5 (about 66 to 98 s for the 254k rung), 25 minutes in all; the box is 60.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-oneq-grid13
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=solo prefill ladder: the protocol fixes its test list, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
